 "relevance_note": "A 123-patient FOXP3-negative IPEX-like cohort in which two patients carry heterozygous TNFAIP3 variants with individual-level detail: \"| S027 | TNFAIP3 | c.1127delC, p.S376fs\" and \"| S087 | TNFAIP3 | c.G2300A, p.C767Y\".",
 "method_note": "Read the whole Markdown by hand; rows were typed into a small Python script (no automatic table transcription) and every span checked verbatim by script. In scope: only S027 and S087 (TNFAIP3 rows in Table II and Table III); the other 121 cohort members (other genes or no diagnosis) get no rows; no relatives of S027/S087 are described. n_patients_reported = 2 is counted from the two TNFAIP3 rows; the text never states the number in words. Table II 'Age' column is not defined in the paper (other rows suggest it may be age at referral, e.g. S045 '14 y' but 'Died age 16y'); recorded as age_at_last_evaluation with that caveat. is_proband taken from the cohort-wide statement 'only probands were available for initial analysis'. disease_label_as_stated taken from the cohort definition ('FOXP3-negative IPEX-like disease'); the paper never names A20 haploinsufficiency or HA20. Table II 'Inh' AD is the inheritance mode of the phenotype, not variant origin, so inheritance = not reported; no parental testing is reported for either patient. Table III 'Functional consequence ... evidence for causality' cells for both patients cite mechanism/literature only (no assay), so functional_evidence_statement = not reported. Variant class: S027 from 'p.S376fs' plus 'Truncating mutation' and 'LoF'; S087 'missense' read from the amino-acid substitution p.C767Y (Type column shows only PPH2/gerp scores, no class word). genomic coordinates combine the cell with the 'hg19 position' column header. Pathogenicity from the 'This study' column, with the legend 'P: pathogenic; LP: likely pathogenic'. S027 'autoantibodies to thyroid (without frank thyroiditis)': thyroiditis recorded excluded (checklist autoimmune thyroiditis excluded), though 'frank' could leave subclinical thyroiditis open. Eczema mapped to the skin-lesions checklist item and failure to thrive to growth failure. S087's only clinical feature is '“IPEX”' (recorded as an observed feature with no HPO candidate); it does not resolve any checklist item, so all 20 are not reported. Treatment recommendations are in Table EII and complete genotypes in Table S2, neither of which is in the file. Internal inconsistencies (not affecting TNFAIP3 rows): '56 different variants' vs '58 reported variants'; S045 'gastric adenocarcinoma' in text vs 'intestinal adenocarcinoma' in Table II; 'SDH' (Table II) vs 'SBDH' (Table III).",
